### Framework Details
- **Framework:** Next.js 15.5.23 (App Router)
- **Package Manager:** npm (package-lock.json present)
- **Implementation:** Follows App Router pattern with Analytics component in root layout

### Deployment Notes
According to the official documentation:
1. Deploy the application using `vercel deploy`
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard under the Analytics section
3. Analytics will start tracking on the next deployment

### Additional Features Present
The implementation includes a comment explaining the Analytics component:
"Vercel Web Analytics: visitor counts, no cookies."

This indicates the developer understood that Vercel Web Analytics:
- Provides visitor count tracking
- Is privacy-friendly (no cookies)
- Collects anonymous usage data

### No Changes Required
The project already has Vercel Web Analytics properly installed and configured according to the latest official documentation. The implementation is production-ready and follows Next.js App Router best practices.
